From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: hdmitx21: the audio settle does not unmute a path being prepared, or
 a muted one

Found in review, traced in the code; two problems in 9010's aud_settle_fn:

- The sound driver's prepare (hdmitx_audio_notify_callback: MISC_AUDIO_PREPARE,
  type CT_PREPARE) mutes the samples while it swaps the output path, and
  the hdmitx_set_audmode that follows settles again. A settle still pending
  from the previous format change fired in between and unmuted the unfed
  path - the burst 9010 exists to remove. It now stays muted while the
  current type is CT_PREPARE.
- It unmuted with audio_mute_op(aud_output_en), reading aud_output_en
  without aud_mute_mutex: an HDCP stream mute or a sysfs mute made
  concurrently could be overwritten, leaving the hardware unmuted while
  every path's state said muted. It now unmutes through
  hdmitx21_audio_mute_op(1, 0), which takes the lock and unmutes only when
  no path is muted.

The pending settle is also cancelled in hdmitx_uninit.
---
 drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hw/hdmi_tx_hw.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hw/hdmi_tx_hw.c b/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hw/hdmi_tx_hw.c
index 2504c4a..6195ab4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hw/hdmi_tx_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hw/hdmi_tx_hw.c
@@ -1998,8 +1998,20 @@ static void aud_settle_fn(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct hdmitx_dev *hdev = get_hdmitx21_device();
 
+	/* A prepare since the format change (the sound driver tearing the path
+	 * down to swap it) muted the samples for the swap; the set_audmode that
+	 * follows settles again. Unmuting here put the unfed path on the wire.
+	 */
+	if (hdev->tx_comm.cur_audio_param.type == CT_PREPARE) {
+		HDMITX_INFO("audio format settled, but a prepare is pending: stay muted\n");
+		return;
+	}
 	HDMITX_INFO("audio format settled, unmute allowed\n");
-	audio_mute_op(hdev->tx_comm.cur_audio_param.aud_output_en);
+	/* Through the path mask, under its lock: reading aud_output_en unlocked
+	 * could overwrite an HDCP stream mute or a sysfs mute made meanwhile.
+	 * Path 0 changes no path; it unmutes only if none is muted.
+	 */
+	hdmitx21_audio_mute_op(1, 0);
 }
 
 static DECLARE_DELAYED_WORK(aud_settle_work, aud_settle_fn);
@@ -2196,6 +2208,7 @@ static void hdmitx_uninit(struct hdmitx_hw_common *tx_hw)
 	struct hdmitx_dev *hdev = get_hdmitx21_device();
 
 	free_irq(hdev->irq_hpd, (void *)hdev);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&aud_settle_work);
 	HDMITX_DEBUG("power off hdmi, unmux hpd\n");
 
 	fifo_flow_enable_intrs(0);
